; Axiom 7 folding .a onto --cd and .c onto --vm: the cubic has three real
; common tangents and every one of them cuts the sheet, so the
; paper-incidence filter settles nothing and the ambiguity stands.

paper square
mark --vm = map .a onto .b                ; vertical midline x = 1/2
--x = map .a onto --cd and .c onto --vm

; expect error "3 folds place .a onto --cd and .c onto --vm, all landing on the paper; add 'toward .x'"
